WEBVTT

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:03.533
[TERRY]
Get back! Stay away from me!

00:00:05.575 --> 00:00:10.075
[VALERIE] Let her go!
Release the hostage now!

00:00:10.158 --> 00:00:11.700
There's no way, cop!

00:00:11.783 --> 00:00:14.408
Come closer...
and she's history!

00:00:14.492 --> 00:00:16.492
Ya hear?

00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:17.950
It's the end of the line.

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:19.533
So give up. Or die!

00:00:19.617 --> 00:00:21.367
--[TERRY gasps]
--[gunshot]

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.700
[GIRL shrieks]

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:34.283
[MIA] My name is Mia Fey,
attorney-at-law.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.867
And this is the story of the
first time I tried a murder case

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.950
as a defense lawyer.

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:42.242
These events transpired
one year before I met

00:00:42.325 --> 00:00:44.867
my protégé, Phoenix Wright.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.200
The client was
quite a challenging one.

00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:49.908
An escaped death row inmate.

00:00:49.992 --> 00:00:51.117
[MIA]
Hmm...

00:00:52.492 --> 00:00:54.075
[yelps]

00:00:54.158 --> 00:00:56.158
The layers of this trial
would coalesce,

00:00:56.242 --> 00:00:58.408
forming a much larger picture.

00:00:58.492 --> 00:01:00.742
Revealing a shocking
truth I'd carry with me

00:01:00.825 --> 00:01:02.783
for the rest of my life.

00:02:34.825 --> 00:02:36.492
[MIA whimpers]

00:02:36.575 --> 00:02:39.158
Feels like my heart's
gonna beat outta my chest.

00:02:39.242 --> 00:02:42.908
You can do this, Mia!
Pull yourself together!

00:02:42.992 --> 00:02:44.992
--Good Morning!
--[bellows]

00:02:45.075 --> 00:02:46.325
[screams]

00:02:46.408 --> 00:02:47.825
Sorry, I really didn't
mean to startle you!

00:02:47.908 --> 00:02:49.158
I was just trying
to be friendly!

00:02:49.242 --> 00:02:52.450
[TERRY] I din't do nuttin'!
I din't kill nobody!

00:02:52.533 --> 00:02:53.950
[gasps]

00:02:59.158 --> 00:03:01.408
[MIA] This is my first client,
Terry Fawles.

00:03:01.492 --> 00:03:03.950
Sentenced to death
five years ago for murder.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:05.367
He escaped from prison,

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.825
and now faces
another murder charge.

00:03:07.908 --> 00:03:11.283
[TERRY grunts] I din't do
nuttin' to nobody, I swear it!

00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:14.908
Yes. Of course,
but you did escape from prison.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.158
[TERRY growls]

00:03:17.242 --> 00:03:18.492
[MIA]
I'm sorry! Please calm down!

00:03:19.783 --> 00:03:22.325
[MIA] Two days ago,
his police transport crashed

00:03:22.408 --> 00:03:24.367
and he fled the scene.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:26.950
Eight hours later,
he was recaptured.

00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:31.158
But in that relatively brief
time, a policewoman was killed.

00:03:31.242 --> 00:03:33.950
And once again,
Terry Fawles stands accused.

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:38.242
[TERRY] It's a setup.
Just like the last time.

00:03:38.325 --> 00:03:40.658
That woman didn't tell
the truth about me.

00:03:40.742 --> 00:03:43.075
I had to. I...

00:03:43.158 --> 00:03:46.950
You had to escape... and
meet up with the policewoman?

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:50.283
[TERRY whimpers]
Yeah. That's the reason

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:53.367
I busted out. But...

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:54.367
[gasps]

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.742
I din't kill her! I swear!

00:03:57.825 --> 00:03:59.492
[MIA gasps]

00:03:59.575 --> 00:04:03.450
[MIA] I have to trust my client.
It's the only way.

00:04:03.533 --> 00:04:06.200
[DIEGO]
Heh. If you wanna build a case,

00:04:06.283 --> 00:04:09.158
you'll have to do more
than just stare at the guy

00:04:09.242 --> 00:04:10.825
So, this is the
cub's first foray

00:04:10.908 --> 00:04:13.242
into the lion's den, huh?

00:04:13.325 --> 00:04:15.033
I gotta see this.

00:04:15.117 --> 00:04:17.033
Mister Armando!

00:04:17.117 --> 00:04:19.908
You've got some
impressive guts, Ms. Fey.

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:22.492
I've never seen somebody
take on a death row escapee

00:04:22.575 --> 00:04:23.867
as their first client.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.783
Not sure we can
chalk it up to guts.

00:04:25.867 --> 00:04:28.825
Now, now.
I admire your boldness.

00:04:28.908 --> 00:04:31.158
Pairs well with
one more seasoned.

00:04:31.242 --> 00:04:32.283
[gasps]

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:33.742
So, Ms. Fey.

00:04:33.825 --> 00:04:35.617
Do you not prefer
a strong blend?

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.200
No, it's great!

00:04:37.283 --> 00:04:39.575
I'm just surprised they sent the
number-one lawyer in the firm

00:04:39.658 --> 00:04:41.450
to help me out with
this case, is all

00:04:41.533 --> 00:04:44.283
Heh. Well, today,
you're the number one.

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:46.158
The cream does rise to the top.

00:04:47.783 --> 00:04:50.700
[DIEGO slurps]
If we wanna start discussing

00:04:50.783 --> 00:04:53.533
the facts of the case,
our friend here met the victim

00:04:53.617 --> 00:04:55.367
two days ago.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:58.617
This memo found on her desk
is the first piece of evidence.

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.200
[TERRY whimpers]

00:05:00.283 --> 00:05:02.200
[DIEGO] He called
and requested a meeting.

00:05:02.283 --> 00:05:05.825
Specified time and place, and
even asked for an identifier.

00:05:05.908 --> 00:05:08.117
[MIA]
Wear a white scarf?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:12.158
A person's appearance
can change a lot in five years.

00:05:12.242 --> 00:05:15.158
[MIA] The circumstantial
evidence is damning.

00:05:15.242 --> 00:05:17.158
How am I gonna turn this around?

00:05:17.242 --> 00:05:20.908
Relax, counselor.
The prosecutor's a baby.

00:05:20.992 --> 00:05:22.867
Practically fresh
out of his diapers.

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:24.992
What? His first case, too?

00:05:25.075 --> 00:05:26.492
[DIEGO] But... He's
already being hailed as

00:05:26.575 --> 00:05:28.492
the greatest prodigy
the prosecutor's office

00:05:28.575 --> 00:05:30.200
has ever seen.

00:05:30.283 --> 00:05:31.325
Is he?

00:05:31.408 --> 00:05:33.533
Well, better
sharpen those claws!

00:05:33.617 --> 00:05:35.200
The lion's den awaits.

00:05:35.283 --> 00:05:36.742
[MIA whimpers]

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:45.075
Order, Court is in session
for the trial of Terry Fawles.

00:05:45.158 --> 00:05:47.700
Your Honor, the
defense is ready to begin.

00:05:47.783 --> 00:05:50.283
Of course,
I am ready, Your Honor.

00:05:50.367 --> 00:05:53.075
Ahem. I've been told,
that both lawyers

00:05:53.158 --> 00:05:56.158
have never tried a case.
Please introduce yourselves.

00:05:56.242 --> 00:05:59.533
Uh... Yes.
Your Honor, I'm Mia Fey.

00:05:59.617 --> 00:06:02.242
I am Miles Edgeworth,
Your Honor.

00:06:02.325 --> 00:06:04.617
Oh. I've actually
been hearing quite a bit

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.700
about you, Mister Edgeworth.

00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:09.158
A prosecutor of your
young age is a first.

00:06:09.242 --> 00:06:10.408
I am 20.

00:06:10.492 --> 00:06:12.742
[MIA]
He's younger than me?

00:06:12.825 --> 00:06:14.283
Wow. That's so young.

00:06:14.367 --> 00:06:16.825
I suppose you're still brewing
up your reputation, Ms. Fey.

00:06:16.908 --> 00:06:17.950
[MIA growls]

00:06:20.242 --> 00:06:21.992
[JUDGE 204A]
Well, Prosecutor Edgeworth.

00:06:22.075 --> 00:06:23.700
Your opening statement, please.

00:06:24.742 --> 00:06:28.033
Just five years ago,
this man, the defendant

00:06:28.117 --> 00:06:30.700
Terry Fawles, was
sentenced to death.

00:06:30.783 --> 00:06:32.283
His crimes were heinous.

00:06:32.367 --> 00:06:36.367
Kidnapping, extortion, and the
murder of a 14 year-old girl,

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:39.033
whose life he took by
throwing her from a bridge.

00:06:39.117 --> 00:06:41.408
Her body was
flung into Eagle River,

00:06:41.492 --> 00:06:44.450
which is well known for
its powerful current.

00:06:44.533 --> 00:06:46.825
A large percentage of
the bodies that have fallen in

00:06:46.908 --> 00:06:48.825
have never been recovered.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:51.117
A truly heinous crime, indeed.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.242
The deciding
factor in that case...

00:06:53.325 --> 00:06:55.200
...was the testimony
of a witness.

00:06:55.283 --> 00:06:57.825
[TERRY whimpers]

00:06:57.908 --> 00:07:00.742
[MILES] It was the officer
who made the arrest.

00:07:00.825 --> 00:07:02.908
She confronted him at
the scene of the crime.

00:07:02.992 --> 00:07:06.200
And her recounting of that
moment is what sealed his fate.

00:07:06.283 --> 00:07:09.242
This monster took
that little girl hostage.

00:07:09.325 --> 00:07:11.325
And then just threw
her in the river!

00:07:11.408 --> 00:07:14.117
[TERRY whimpers]

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.825
[MIA] So her account
is what sealed the deal.

00:07:16.908 --> 00:07:18.700
What put him on death row.

00:07:18.783 --> 00:07:21.158
[MILES]
Sadly, she was his next victim.

00:07:21.242 --> 00:07:23.825
The same brave woman
who refused to back down.

00:07:23.908 --> 00:07:26.242
Police Sergeant
Valerie Hawthorne.

00:07:26.325 --> 00:07:28.700
Her courage and strong
sense of moral obligation

00:07:28.783 --> 00:07:32.075
is what put him away.
So when he escaped...

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.408
...he was hell-bent
on getting revenge!

00:07:37.533 --> 00:07:40.117
It's obvious--
this defendant is guilty.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.783
[MIA gasps]
Wha--?! Hold on, Your Honor!

00:07:42.867 --> 00:07:45.742
A-As the defense, I, uh...

00:07:45.825 --> 00:07:48.075
I demand a cross-examination!

00:07:48.158 --> 00:07:49.658
[JUDGE 204A] Oh, I suppose
youngsters these days

00:07:49.742 --> 00:07:51.950
don't know when to give up.

00:07:52.033 --> 00:07:55.325
I blame naivete, the
glaring inexperience of youth.

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:58.075
[MIA] What the hell? You're
younger than me, you know?

00:07:58.158 --> 00:08:00.367
Very well. In that case,

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.658
I call the detective
overseeing the investigation

00:08:02.742 --> 00:08:04.617
to take the stand.

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:06.742
Please state
your name and occupation.

00:08:06.825 --> 00:08:10.117
Sir! My name's Dick Gumshoe,
and I'm a homicidal--

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:12.617
I mean, a homicide detective
down at the precinct.

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:14.033
Was a beat cop,

00:08:14.117 --> 00:08:17.492
but now... "Big" Dick is
standing tall as a proud member

00:08:17.575 --> 00:08:19.283
of the detective unit!

00:08:19.367 --> 00:08:20.992
I don't believe that's relevant.

00:08:21.075 --> 00:08:23.783
Detective.
Your testimony, please.

00:08:23.867 --> 00:08:25.617
[GUMSHOE]
Yes, Your Majesty!

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.700
[MIA]
This is it! A real trial.

00:08:27.783 --> 00:08:32.367
[DIEGO] Listen closely, kid.
You'll need your full attention.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.408
Or you may find
yourself ground up...

00:08:34.492 --> 00:08:37.617
[slurps]
...and then roasted by justice.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:39.242
[MIA growls]

00:08:39.325 --> 00:08:41.617
[GUMSHOE clears throat]
The day of the incident,

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.783
the defendant called the victim.

00:08:43.867 --> 00:08:46.117
He asked Officer Hawthorne
if she'd meet with him.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:49.117
She then went to Dusky
Bridge at the designated time

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:51.200
She jotted down
a memo during the call.

00:08:51.283 --> 00:08:52.533
Shown here.

00:08:52.617 --> 00:08:54.950
[MIA] The same one Armando
showed me in the lobby.

00:08:55.033 --> 00:08:56.992
[GUMSHOE] The two met and
the defendant proceeded to stab

00:08:57.075 --> 00:08:59.575
the victim in the back
with a hunting knife.

00:08:59.658 --> 00:09:01.117
The wound would prove fatal.

00:09:02.325 --> 00:09:04.533
[GUMSHOE] He then stuffed her
body into the trunk of his car

00:09:04.617 --> 00:09:06.992
and attempted to make a getaway.

00:09:07.075 --> 00:09:10.575
But he was quickly
arrested at a police checkpoint.

00:09:10.658 --> 00:09:13.200
Here's a photograph
of the victim's body.

00:09:13.283 --> 00:09:17.033
You can clearly see the murder
weapon still lodged in her back.

00:09:17.117 --> 00:09:18.700
It's all pretty cut and dried.

00:09:18.783 --> 00:09:20.367
[CROWD whispering]

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.867
All right, defense.
Your witness.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:24.617
--[MIA gasps]
--[JUDGE 204A] Defense?

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:27.117
Of course! Yep, coming right up!

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:28.658
[DIEGO]
Easy, easy.

00:09:28.742 --> 00:09:29.867
Keep trembling like
that and you're gonna

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:31.408
make me spill my jitter juice.

00:09:31.492 --> 00:09:33.658
[MIA]
I'm just so excited!

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:39.700
So the defendant,
Mister Fawles, had a car?

00:09:39.783 --> 00:09:41.283
[GUMSHOE]
Well, yeah.

00:09:41.367 --> 00:09:43.825
I mean, the murder happened on a
bridge way up in the mountains.

00:09:43.908 --> 00:09:46.492
It was a stolen car, of course.

00:09:46.575 --> 00:09:48.450
A bridge up in the mountains?

00:09:48.533 --> 00:09:50.325
Why would they be meeting there?

00:09:50.408 --> 00:09:51.950
The location's significant.

00:09:52.033 --> 00:09:54.450
Because it factored
heavily in the earlier case.

00:09:54.533 --> 00:09:56.158
[JUDGE 204A]
In what way, exactly?

00:09:56.242 --> 00:09:57.658
It's the crime scene.

00:09:57.742 --> 00:10:00.575
The place he murdered his
young hostage five years ago.

00:10:00.658 --> 00:10:04.158
And was subsequently apprehended
by officer Hawthorne.

00:10:04.242 --> 00:10:06.408
This also transpired
on Dusky Bridge.

00:10:06.492 --> 00:10:09.200
Heh. You're saying he was
looking to have a reunion

00:10:09.283 --> 00:10:10.950
at their special place, right?

00:10:12.075 --> 00:10:15.242
[GUMSHOE] This photograph was
taken moments before the crime.

00:10:15.325 --> 00:10:18.783
You can clearly see the two of
them facing off on the bridge!

00:10:18.867 --> 00:10:19.783
[gasps]

00:10:19.867 --> 00:10:21.325
What a pretty picture.

00:10:21.408 --> 00:10:26.783
Huh, Fey? Hmph. I'd say the
evidence is strong and bitter.

00:10:26.867 --> 00:10:30.533
However, there's an odd taste.

00:10:30.617 --> 00:10:33.617
Something that leaves
me feeling kinda cold.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:35.325
Uh... Odd taste?

00:10:37.075 --> 00:10:39.783
[MIA gasps]
Oh. I see!

00:10:39.867 --> 00:10:41.408
That's good. Now.

00:10:41.492 --> 00:10:44.158
Let's sample that signature
roast of the truth.

00:10:44.242 --> 00:10:45.283
Detective!

00:10:45.367 --> 00:10:46.825
Yes, ma'am?

00:10:46.908 --> 00:10:49.325
You described this
photo as "cut and dried."

00:10:49.408 --> 00:10:50.658
That's what you said, right?

00:10:50.742 --> 00:10:52.450
[GUMSHOE]
Yeah, that sounds like me!

00:10:52.533 --> 00:10:55.367
Look here. At the memo
the victim had written.

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:57.492
"Wear white scarf
for identification."

00:10:57.575 --> 00:10:59.117
If she followed all
the instructions,

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.325
she must've been
wearing a white scarf.

00:11:01.408 --> 00:11:04.033
Except... Upon
further examination.

00:11:04.117 --> 00:11:05.242
[CROWD gasping]

00:11:05.325 --> 00:11:07.575
[GUMSHOE] What the...?!
I don't see a scarf!

00:11:07.658 --> 00:11:09.658
Yes! So...

00:11:12.158 --> 00:11:13.658
Uh, that means...

00:11:13.742 --> 00:11:15.117
Something's messed up!

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:16.742
[GUMSHOE growls, yells]

00:11:16.825 --> 00:11:18.700
[CROWD gasping]

00:11:18.783 --> 00:11:21.367
[DIEGO] I think you meant to
say, there's a "contradiction."

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:23.700
[MILES] Could this be the
scarf you're looking for,

00:11:23.783 --> 00:11:25.158
by any chance?

00:11:25.242 --> 00:11:27.367
Wait! Where the
hell d'ya find that?

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:29.242
On Dusky Bridge, of course.

00:11:29.325 --> 00:11:31.325
It was the first place I looked.

00:11:31.408 --> 00:11:33.867
[GUMSHOE] I don't get why
you wouldn't tell me about it!

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:35.908
[MIA]
Something feels wrong here.

00:11:35.992 --> 00:11:39.117
Did the prosecutor
hide it on purpose?

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:42.158
It's not exactly white,
as the defendant had requested.

00:11:42.242 --> 00:11:44.700
but the victim likely
thought it was close enough.

00:11:44.783 --> 00:11:47.492
But it is clearly shown
in this photograph.

00:11:47.575 --> 00:11:49.075
As she tried to
fight off her killer,

00:11:49.158 --> 00:11:51.575
it slipped from her neck.

00:11:51.658 --> 00:11:54.617
I'm quite shocked...
the defense overlooked it!

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:55.783
[MIA groans]

00:11:55.867 --> 00:11:57.408
[CROWD murmuring]

00:11:57.492 --> 00:11:58.908
[MILES]
Hmph.

00:11:58.992 --> 00:12:00.825
[MIA]
Was this a trap?

00:12:00.908 --> 00:12:04.242
[DIEGO]
Well? Tell me, Ms. Fey.

00:12:04.325 --> 00:12:06.575
Still trust the
death row inmate?

00:12:06.658 --> 00:12:08.867
[TERRY whimpers]

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:10.325
Of course I do!

00:12:10.408 --> 00:12:13.075
Good. I think
we need to refocus.

00:12:13.158 --> 00:12:15.242
Maybe listen to
some new testimony.

00:12:15.325 --> 00:12:17.617
What? New testimony?

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:18.700
From whom?

00:12:18.783 --> 00:12:20.950
We'll have to find that witness.

00:12:21.033 --> 00:12:23.158
The one with the camera.

00:12:23.242 --> 00:12:24.908
[MIA gasps]
Detective!

00:12:24.992 --> 00:12:25.908
[gasps]

00:12:25.992 --> 00:12:27.367
This photo you provided.

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:29.117
Can you produce
the individual who took it?

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:31.700
[GUMSHOE]
Huh? I... Well, uh...

00:12:31.783 --> 00:12:35.033
The photograph in question,
was taken by a third party.

00:12:35.117 --> 00:12:37.242
In other words, an eyewitness.

00:12:37.325 --> 00:12:39.325
Can you tell me why they
haven't been summoned?

00:12:39.408 --> 00:12:41.825
If there was in fact
a witness to this crime,

00:12:41.908 --> 00:12:44.742
the defense demands they
provide sworn testimony!

00:12:44.825 --> 00:12:46.992
[CROWD gasping, murmuring]

00:12:47.075 --> 00:12:49.408
The prosecution has
no desire to hide the witness

00:12:49.492 --> 00:12:51.242
from this court.
To the contrary,

00:12:51.325 --> 00:12:53.742
we're prepared to hear
their statement at any time!

00:12:53.825 --> 00:12:56.117
Oh. That's very brave.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:13:00.492
[MILES] The prosecution hereby
summons... the courageous woman

00:13:00.575 --> 00:13:02.533
who witnessed the
tragic events of that day

00:13:02.617 --> 00:13:04.408
with her very own eyes!

00:13:13.325 --> 00:13:14.658
[MILES] Witness,
would you please state

00:13:14.742 --> 00:13:16.867
your name and occupation?

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:18.575
Of course, sir.

00:13:18.658 --> 00:13:23.033
My name is Melissa Foster.
And I'm a college student.

00:13:23.117 --> 00:13:25.367
It's my pleasure
to meet you all.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.325
Ahh! I see an angel!

00:13:28.408 --> 00:13:30.658
Positively radiant! Such grace.

00:13:30.742 --> 00:13:33.950
Like my verdict will be decided
by divine intervention.

00:13:34.033 --> 00:13:35.283
[MIA]
What an idiot!

00:13:35.367 --> 00:13:37.742
[DIEGO] Hmph. Well,
I see a cloud darker

00:13:37.825 --> 00:13:39.825
than a triple espresso.

00:13:39.908 --> 00:13:42.700
You were on the scene
that day, were you not?

00:13:42.783 --> 00:13:44.783
When this terrible
event occurred?

00:13:44.867 --> 00:13:46.033
[MELISSA]
Mm-hmm...

00:13:46.117 --> 00:13:47.658
Is it accurate
to state you're the one

00:13:47.742 --> 00:13:48.992
who took this photo?

00:13:50.492 --> 00:13:53.908
[MELISSA] Um... Excuse me,
but who might you be?

00:13:53.992 --> 00:13:56.117
Oh. I'm the defense lawyer.

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:58.117
My name is Mia Fey.

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:01.867
[MELISSA]
Fey, huh? So, it is you.

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:03.033
[MIA gasps]

00:14:03.117 --> 00:14:04.533
[JUDGE 204A]
Now then, young lady.

00:14:04.617 --> 00:14:07.075
If you're ready, please
begin your testimony

00:14:07.158 --> 00:14:09.992
[MELISSA] Of course.
I'd be more than happy to.

00:14:12.033 --> 00:14:14.575
[MELISSA] That day... I'd
taken my camera and tripod

00:14:14.658 --> 00:14:17.325
to this charming, flowery,
little meadow that also had

00:14:17.408 --> 00:14:19.033
a view of the bridge.

00:14:19.117 --> 00:14:21.867
[MELISSA] Using the timer, I took
some cute pictures of myself

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:23.700
frolicking amongst
the butterflies

00:14:23.783 --> 00:14:25.450
and beautiful cherry blossoms.

00:14:25.533 --> 00:14:27.617
[giggles]

00:14:28.742 --> 00:14:30.075
[MELISSA]
Hmm?

00:14:30.158 --> 00:14:31.367
[MELISSA] I couldn't help
but notice there was a man

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.742
and a woman having
an encounter on the bridge.

00:14:33.825 --> 00:14:36.075
My interest was piqued,
but as I watched them,

00:14:36.158 --> 00:14:38.492
they began to scuffle
and tussle with each other.

00:14:38.575 --> 00:14:39.950
[gasps]

00:14:40.033 --> 00:14:41.867
[MELISSA] Miss Victim tried
to skedaddle out of there,

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:43.533
and rushed past Mister Killer.

00:14:43.617 --> 00:14:45.075
As her back was to him,
he followed her

00:14:45.158 --> 00:14:47.533
and gored her like a bull!

00:14:47.617 --> 00:14:49.492
[screams]

00:14:49.575 --> 00:14:51.158
[MELISSA] Then, big
Mister Killer picked up

00:14:51.242 --> 00:14:54.367
poor Miss Victim's cadaver
and carried it off the bridge.

00:14:56.075 --> 00:14:57.408
[MELISSA]
From what I understand,

00:14:57.492 --> 00:14:59.492
he hid it in the trunk
of this automobile

00:14:59.575 --> 00:15:02.325
like it was some kind of
refuse and fled the scene.

00:15:02.408 --> 00:15:04.658
When I finally returned
to my senses,

00:15:04.742 --> 00:15:06.742
I telephoned the boys in blue.

00:15:06.825 --> 00:15:08.867
[JUDGE 204A] Hmm.
Witnessing such violence

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:10.450
must've been traumatizing.

00:15:10.533 --> 00:15:12.242
[MELISSA]
It's true. I feared my little

00:15:12.325 --> 00:15:15.283
heart would go pitter-patter
right out of my chest.

00:15:15.367 --> 00:15:17.742
[JUDGE 204A]
Mm. You poor delicate flower.

00:15:17.825 --> 00:15:19.950
If her testimony
is allowed to stand,

00:15:20.033 --> 00:15:21.033
we'll be burned.

00:15:21.117 --> 00:15:22.658
Oh, no!

00:15:22.742 --> 00:15:26.325
[MIA]
Okay, Mia, time to fight back.

00:15:26.408 --> 00:15:28.533
[MIA] You claim the killer
picked up the victim's body

00:15:28.617 --> 00:15:31.700
and carried her off.
Are you absolutely certain?

00:15:31.783 --> 00:15:32.908
Yes.

00:15:32.992 --> 00:15:35.367
[MIA] Hmm, it's rather odd,
don't you think?

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:36.825
Huh?

00:15:36.908 --> 00:15:39.658
[MIA] I mean, considering
the river under the bridge.

00:15:39.742 --> 00:15:43.117
If he wanted to hide it, why not
just throw it into the current?

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.325
[gasps]

00:15:44.408 --> 00:15:46.825
In fact... This same
man was proven guilty

00:15:46.908 --> 00:15:49.533
of doing exactly that
only five years ago!

00:15:49.617 --> 00:15:50.867
[gasps]

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.658
[MIA] So why would he choose
to carry a dead body

00:15:52.742 --> 00:15:54.867
all the way to
his car this time?

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:56.033
It doesn't make sense!

00:15:56.117 --> 00:15:58.367
[MELISSA]
Uh... Well, I...

00:15:58.450 --> 00:16:00.158
His judgment is not in question!

00:16:00.242 --> 00:16:03.158
He is being tried here
today for his brutal actions!

00:16:03.242 --> 00:16:04.825
She did not read his mind,

00:16:04.908 --> 00:16:06.950
but she did see him
kill that woman!

00:16:07.033 --> 00:16:08.325
Yes, without a doubt.

00:16:08.408 --> 00:16:09.992
I saw him do it!

00:16:10.075 --> 00:16:12.075
He carried her off, and then
he broke into the trunk

00:16:12.158 --> 00:16:14.408
of the car where
hid her lifeless body!

00:16:14.492 --> 00:16:15.700
[MIA gasps]

00:16:15.783 --> 00:16:17.158
That would impossible!

00:16:17.242 --> 00:16:19.325
Uh, what do you mean by that?

00:16:19.408 --> 00:16:21.450
This is one of your
photos from that day.

00:16:21.533 --> 00:16:23.367
I ask you to look carefully.

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.283
Notice that the end
of the bridge is hidden

00:16:25.367 --> 00:16:27.283
behind this outcropping.

00:16:27.367 --> 00:16:30.033
Which means from where
you were standing...

00:16:30.117 --> 00:16:32.492
...you couldn't have seen
him breaking into that car!

00:16:32.575 --> 00:16:34.158
[wails]

00:16:34.242 --> 00:16:35.658
If you didn't witness it,

00:16:35.742 --> 00:16:38.450
then explain how you know
about that specific detail!

00:16:38.533 --> 00:16:41.283
Logically, there's only one
answer that would make sense.

00:16:41.367 --> 00:16:42.658
[MELISSA whimpers]

00:16:42.742 --> 00:16:44.117
[MIA] The person who placed
officer Hawthorne's body

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:46.450
in the trunk of that car...

00:16:46.533 --> 00:16:48.992
...was the witness,
Melissa Foster!

00:16:49.075 --> 00:16:51.200
[JUDGE 204A] Hold on.
What reason would she have

00:16:51.283 --> 00:16:52.283
to hide the body?

00:16:52.367 --> 00:16:54.200
[MILES]
Objection!

00:16:54.283 --> 00:16:56.033
There's no way that
she was involved!

00:16:56.117 --> 00:16:58.325
She wasn't present
at the actual scene!

00:16:58.408 --> 00:16:59.825
Have you forgotten?

00:16:59.908 --> 00:17:02.700
She took this photograph exactly
when the murder happened!

00:17:02.783 --> 00:17:04.908
It seems to me
you have forgotten

00:17:04.992 --> 00:17:06.450
the witness' testimony.

00:17:06.533 --> 00:17:08.325
She was using
a tripod and a timer.

00:17:08.408 --> 00:17:09.658
[MILES gasps]

00:17:09.742 --> 00:17:11.992
Therefore... the camera
could've taken the picture

00:17:12.075 --> 00:17:14.242
with or without her
behind the lens.

00:17:14.325 --> 00:17:18.408
[MILES growls] Okay. But why
would she do all that?

00:17:21.283 --> 00:17:23.533
[MIA] Because she murdered
Valerie Hawthorne,

00:17:23.617 --> 00:17:25.325
and then hid the
body in the trunk.

00:17:25.408 --> 00:17:27.117
What? I would never.

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:28.825
This would also
explain why the body

00:17:28.908 --> 00:17:30.283
was not dumped in the river.

00:17:30.367 --> 00:17:33.242
It was all a plot to
frame Mister Fawles!

00:17:33.325 --> 00:17:37.325
[MELISSA gasps, screams]

00:17:37.408 --> 00:17:40.825
[JUDGE 204A] Wait a minute!
The witness is the real killer?

00:17:40.908 --> 00:17:42.742
It just don't make no sense!

00:17:42.825 --> 00:17:43.992
What's wrong with that?

00:17:44.075 --> 00:17:45.450
[TERRY]
Well... What happened was...

00:17:45.533 --> 00:17:47.325
I got in that car
and drove away,

00:17:47.408 --> 00:17:48.783
right after I met the lady.

00:17:48.867 --> 00:17:50.575
So there wasn't
no time to kill her

00:17:50.658 --> 00:17:52.242
and put her in the trunk.

00:17:52.325 --> 00:17:54.783
I see. Which would
imply that the killer

00:17:54.867 --> 00:17:57.742
hid the victim's body in
the trunk before you two

00:17:57.825 --> 00:17:58.908
met on the bridge.

00:17:58.992 --> 00:18:00.992
Further proving
that you were framed.

00:18:01.075 --> 00:18:02.992
[MILES]
Objection!

00:18:03.075 --> 00:18:05.158
This is asinine!

00:18:05.242 --> 00:18:06.867
Everyone here can
clearly see that the victim

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:08.283
is in the photograph!

00:18:08.367 --> 00:18:10.242
Which means Valerie
Hawthorne was, indeed,

00:18:10.325 --> 00:18:12.200
alive when it was taken!

00:18:12.283 --> 00:18:13.867
Objection!

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:15.408
[MILES groans]

00:18:15.492 --> 00:18:17.075
[MIA] Mister Edgeworth,
are you unwilling

00:18:17.158 --> 00:18:18.283
or unable to understand?

00:18:18.367 --> 00:18:19.617
[MILES gasps]

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:22.033
By the time my client
had arrived at the bridge,

00:18:22.117 --> 00:18:24.950
the victim was dead and
her body had been hidden.

00:18:25.033 --> 00:18:27.117
Ergo, the person
in the photograph

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:28.992
was not Valerie Hawthorne.

00:18:29.075 --> 00:18:32.742
[MILES] Absurd! If not her,
who else could it have been?

00:18:32.825 --> 00:18:34.575
[MIA]
That should be obvious.

00:18:34.658 --> 00:18:35.825
[MILES]

00:18:35.908 --> 00:18:39.117
[MIA] It was your "eyewitness,"
Melissa Foster!

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:41.408
[MILES]
No! That cannot be!

00:18:41.492 --> 00:18:43.575
[CROWD]

00:18:43.658 --> 00:18:45.700
[TERRY]

00:18:45.783 --> 00:18:47.742
[JUDGE 204A] You think
she was posing as the victim?

00:18:47.825 --> 00:18:50.617
[MIA] It was you on that bridge,
wasn't it, Miss Foster?

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:53.367
You staged this.

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:55.242
[DIEGO]
Now there's that boldness.

00:18:55.325 --> 00:18:57.075
Really hits the spot.

00:18:57.158 --> 00:18:59.783
[MELISSA]
That's a lie! It's preposterous!

00:18:59.867 --> 00:19:03.408
Why would I disguise myself to
look like Miss Victim?

00:19:03.492 --> 00:19:04.867
[MIA] Mister Fawles
had trouble remembering

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:06.867
the victim's appearance.

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:10.575
That's why he needed the
scarf as a way to identify her.

00:19:10.658 --> 00:19:11.617
Correct?

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:14.700
[TERRY]
Uh, yeah. I forgot her face.

00:19:14.783 --> 00:19:16.867
[JUDGE 204A]
So... You truly forgot?

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:20.283
[MIA] And thus, if they wore
a scarf, as he'd requested.

00:19:20.367 --> 00:19:21.950
Almost any woman
could've pretended

00:19:22.033 --> 00:19:23.533
to be Valerie Hawthorne!

00:19:23.617 --> 00:19:27.992
[CROWD murmuring]

00:19:28.075 --> 00:19:29.950
This is so cruel!

00:19:30.033 --> 00:19:33.908
All I wanted... was to take
pictures of pretty things.

00:19:33.992 --> 00:19:36.658
I don't know Miss Victim
or Mister Killer.

00:19:36.742 --> 00:19:39.658
I was forced to
witness a horrible crime.

00:19:39.742 --> 00:19:41.867
And you call me a murderer?

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:44.492
I don't know if I'll
be able to bear this shame!

00:19:44.575 --> 00:19:47.325
I am appalled!
There's no motive.

00:19:47.408 --> 00:19:50.158
And you dare to accuse her
of something so monstrous?

00:19:50.242 --> 00:19:53.658
Yes! What reason
would I have to kill her?

00:19:53.742 --> 00:19:55.408
[JUDGE 204A]
Can you answer that, defense?

00:19:55.492 --> 00:19:56.783
What was the motive?

00:19:56.867 --> 00:19:58.575
Well, it's because...

00:19:58.658 --> 00:20:02.825
[MELISSA] Hmph. The killer is
that awful man over there.

00:20:02.908 --> 00:20:04.658
He ripped that
woman's life from her.

00:20:04.742 --> 00:20:07.700
Exactly like he killed
that girl five years ago!

00:20:07.783 --> 00:20:09.492
[DIEGO]
Five years ago?

00:20:09.575 --> 00:20:12.992
When he took the life of
Miss Dahlia Hawthorne, right?

00:20:13.075 --> 00:20:14.742
[MELISSA gulps]

00:20:14.825 --> 00:20:16.783
Dahlia... Hawthorne?

00:20:16.867 --> 00:20:19.158
Yeah. That was her name.

00:20:19.242 --> 00:20:20.867
The poor little girl
who was kidnapped and

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:22.533
murdered five years ago.

00:20:22.617 --> 00:20:24.242
[TERRY whimpers]

00:20:24.325 --> 00:20:26.408
Wait, is that really true?

00:20:26.492 --> 00:20:27.575
Well, does that mean...?

00:20:27.658 --> 00:20:29.700
Yep. And I'm
actually surprised

00:20:29.783 --> 00:20:32.242
that this bit of info
didn't come up sooner.

00:20:32.325 --> 00:20:35.533
Dahlia Hawthorne...
was the victim's younger sister.

00:20:35.617 --> 00:20:36.533
[JUDGE 204A]
What?

00:20:36.617 --> 00:20:38.117
She was?

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:40.700
[MIA] It did strike me as
extremely risky to fire

00:20:40.783 --> 00:20:43.200
at someone holding a hostage.

00:20:43.283 --> 00:20:45.367
And that was her sister.

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:48.867
[gasps] That file,
is that what I think it is?

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:53.200
This? It's all about Mr. Fawles'
previous murder trial.

00:20:53.283 --> 00:20:55.033
I thought the key
to solving this current case

00:20:55.117 --> 00:20:57.158
was probably somewhere in here.

00:20:57.242 --> 00:21:00.367
All we had to do
was look for it.

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:01.783
Objection!

00:21:01.867 --> 00:21:03.867
The name of your client's
last victim is irrelevant!

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:06.367
It has absolutely nothing
to do with this case!

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:08.075
[DIEGO]
I just have to wonder...

00:21:08.158 --> 00:21:09.867
Did she really die?

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:11.700
What are you getting at here?

00:21:11.783 --> 00:21:13.075
This says...

00:21:13.158 --> 00:21:16.117
Five years ago on that
same rickety bridge,

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:19.033
the then 14 year-old
Dahlia Hawthorne

00:21:19.117 --> 00:21:21.742
fell into the river and
her body was never found.

00:21:21.825 --> 00:21:23.492
--[gasps]
--Is that so?

00:21:23.575 --> 00:21:24.992
Sadly...

00:21:25.075 --> 00:21:27.742
...she disappeared from the
world, leaving nary a trace.

00:21:27.825 --> 00:21:28.950
[CROWD murmuring]

00:21:29.033 --> 00:21:30.867
[MIA gasps]

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:33.408
[MIA]
No, it can't be.

00:21:33.492 --> 00:21:35.617
[DIEGO]
She was 14 at the time.

00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:38.200
Which means that if
she were still alive...

00:21:38.283 --> 00:21:40.158
...she'd be around your age.

00:21:40.242 --> 00:21:42.408
[gasps]

00:21:42.492 --> 00:21:45.450
Tell the truth. Who are you?

00:21:45.533 --> 00:21:46.908
What are you hiding?

00:23:20.367 --> 00:23:21.575
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:21.658 --> 00:23:23.533
In order to prove that
her client was innocent.

00:23:23.617 --> 00:23:25.450
Mia had to unravel
the mystery surrounding

00:23:25.533 --> 00:23:27.158
his previous murder conviction.

00:23:27.242 --> 00:23:30.408
What really happened on
that bridge five years ago?

00:23:30.492 --> 00:23:33.325
Exactly who is this
mysterious Melissa Foster?

00:23:33.408 --> 00:23:35.867
And what was Fawles' true
motivation that would lead him

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:37.742
to kill Valerie Hawthorne?

00:23:37.825 --> 00:23:39.700
What will be revealed
when we shine a light

00:23:39.783 --> 00:23:41.283
into this darkness?

00:23:41.367 --> 00:23:43.783
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:43.867 --> 00:23:47.075
Next episode: "Turnabout
Beginnings - Last Trial"!

00:23:47.158 --> 00:23:48.242
Take that!
